---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Circuit from '../components/Circuit.astro';
import {
  project,
  currentRelease as release,
  docsHref,
  downloadHref,
  sourceHref,
} from '../data/project';
---

<Layout title="Two systems. One circuit.">
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <span class="small-line"></span> CREATE COMPATIBILITY, CONNECTED.
      </p>
      <h1>
        Two systems.
        <br />
        <span class="text-mint">One circuit.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        Your factory shouldn't stop
        <br class="desktop-break" /> where one mod ends.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-detail">
        World-Wide Power Grid connects{' '}
        <strong>Create: Electro Energetics</strong> and{' '}
        <strong>Power Grid</strong>. Build mixed stationary circuits with the
        equipment, wires, and controls you already know.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button-mint" href={downloadHref()}>
          Get WWPG <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
        <a class="button button-outline" href={docsHref()}>
          Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note mono">
        {release.version} <span> / </span> API {release.api?.version} AVAILABLE
      </p>
    </div>
    <Circuit />
  </section>
  <div class="spec-strip">
    <div class="container spec-inner">
      <span class="mono">THE FOUNDATION</span>
      <span>
        Minecraft <strong>{release.requirements.Minecraft}</strong>
      </span>
      <span>
        NeoForge <strong>{release.requirements.NeoForge}</strong>
      </span>
      <span>
        Java <strong>{release.requirements.Java}</strong>
      </span>
      <a href="/downloads/">
        All dependencies <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section container" id="connection">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / CONNECT THE POSSIBILITIES</p>
        <h2>
          Same tools.
          <br />A bigger system.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        A CEE supply. A Power Grid board.
        <br />A factory that works across both.
        <br />
        Keep the native workflow. Connect the circuit.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bridge-story">
      <article>
        <span class="mono brass">01.1 / ELECTRO ENERGETICS</span>
        <h3>Prepare the models.</h3>
        <p>
          CEE keeps its equipment, controls, heat, protection, and gameplay.
          WWPG brings its prepared electrical models into the shared circuit.
        </p>
      </article>
      <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        →
      </div>
      <article class="bridge-core">
        <span class="mono text-mint">01.2 / WORLD-WIDE POWER GRID</span>
        <h3>Bridge the systems.</h3>
        <p>
          Persistent circuit elements connect the two mods under one synchronous
          prepare → solve → commit schedule.
        </p>
      </article>
      <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        →
      </div>
      <article>
        <span class="mono violet">01.3 / POWER GRID</span>
        <h3>Solve the circuit.</h3>
        <p>
          PG solves the electrical network. CEE consumes the results for its
          machines and displays. Native and Java backends are supported.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="capabilities-section section" id="capabilities">
    <div class="container capabilities-layout">
      <div class="capabilities-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / BUILD ACROSS THE BOUNDARY</p>
        <h2>
          Power the whole
          <br />
          workshop.
        </h2>
        <p>
          From a relay switching a lamp to storage, transformers, and processing
          equipment.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${docsHref()}compatibility/`}>
          Explore supported content <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <div class="terminal-note mono">
          <span>SUPPORTED IN THIS RELEASE</span>
          <strong>STATIONARY SYSTEMS</strong>
          <span>PINNED VERSIONS / NATIVE WORKFLOWS</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-list">
        <article>
          <span class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            ϟ
          </span>
          <div>
            <span class="mono">GENERATION & STORAGE</span>
            <h3>Make it. Store it. Use it.</h3>
            <p>
              Generate electricity, charge storage, and power supported motors,
              pumps, lamps, and heaters across both mods.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            ⌁
          </span>
          <div>
            <span class="mono">TRANSFORMERS & CONVERSION</span>
            <h3>Shape the supply.</h3>
            <p>
              Build transformer and variac circuits, regulate voltage, use FE
              converters, and link stationary Nether transformers.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="capability-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            ⊞
          </span>
          <div>
            <span class="mono">BOARDS & PANELS</span>
            <h3>Give your factory a control room.</h3>
            <p>
              Use native circuit boards and CEE panels. Save, copy, and assemble
              designs; switch, measure, and protect mixed circuits.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container yard-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / LEARN BY CONNECTING</p>
      <h2>
        Step into
        <br />
        the test yard.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Download a stationary world with working exhibits, signs, tools,
        expected readings, and reset instructions. Follow a circuit. Flip a
        switch. See what changes.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button-outline" href={`${docsHref()}example-worlds/`}>
          Explore the exhibits ↗
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/downloads/#worlds">
          Get the worlds ↓
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="yard-board">
      <div class="mono board-heading">STATIONARY YARD / FIELD NOTES</div>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <span class="mono">S61</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Save a board design.</strong>
            <p>Edit, save, copy, assemble, and power a native circuit board.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mono">S65</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Follow power through the Nether.</strong>
            <p>
              Visit a stationary link with both transformer ends kept loaded.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="mono">S80–81</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Let a computer take control.</strong>
            <p>
              The optional Pinout yard switches eight pins and reads signed
              voltage.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link" href={sourceHref('docs/STATIONARY_YARD.md')}>
        Release-pinned yard guide ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="ecosystem-section container">
    <div class="ecosystem-label mono">04 / BUILD ON THE CONNECTION</div>
    <div class="ecosystem-content">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow violet">FOR ADDON AUTHORS</p>
        <h2>
          More connections.
          <br />
          More possibilities.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Build stationary machines and instruments with immutable electrical
          models, extend custom CEE properties, or bring PG's native board
          components into mixed circuits.
        </p>
        <p class="api-status">
          <span class="status-outline"></span> API {release.api?.version} is
          available with WWPG {release.version}: two SDK contracts, generated
          reference, and independently buildable example addons.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${docsHref()}developers/`}>
          Build your first addon ↗
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href={`/api/${release.version}/`}>
          Java API reference ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container final-invitation">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT CIRCUIT STARTS HERE</p>
      <h2>
        Connect something
        <br />
        worth figuring out.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a class="button button-mint" href="/downloads/">
        Get started with WWPG ↗
      </a>
      <p class="small-text">Check the pinned dependencies before installing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="attribution container">
    <p>
      Built on{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/george8188625/Create-Electro-Energetics">
        Create: Electro Energetics
      </a>{' '}
      and <a href="https://github.com/patryk3211/PowerGrid">Power Grid</a>. Each
      project retains ownership of its native content. WWPG's own code and
      documentation are{' '}
      <a href={`${project.repository}/blob/${release.commit}/LICENSE`}>
        MIT licensed
      </a>
      ; bundled PG native resources retain Apache 2.0 attribution.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
